  "contract": [
    "Clear five workspace buffers, initialize the dual-history filter descriptor and clear both histories, then reset the exact state fields and interleaved workspace history words. Preserve all other state bytes.",
    "Load the saved allocation only when calling free, even for null, leave that pointer unchanged after free, then store status0xbf and return0.",
    "Filter initializer stores six descriptor words in stock order and clears each history with32-bit wrapped count*4+4 length. Preserve floating-point scale bits without arithmetic.",
    "Basic ADT resets bytes2 then0 and preserves byte1. Soft ADT resets the timeout after its parent returns, for both success and failure, and normalizes nonzero status to-1."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "All278 native entry instruction bytes execute across the direct and modeled-status fixtures. Direct zero/free ports snapshot state and clobber caller scratch. Real C fill comparisons check actual byte writes; heap integration executes real C initialization/malloc/free and the reset/public soft adapter with no stock-code fallback.",
    "Filter histories are valid caller-owned buffers for the wrapped byte lengths tested. Overlapping buffers, descriptor/history aliasing, four byte alignments, finite/infinite/NaN/signed-zero bits and selected wrapped counts are tested. Invalid null history behavior for positive lengths is outside the contract.",
    "FP context is primed by an isolated fixture VMOV before setting per-call FP registers/FPSCR. An initial diagnostic observed lazy FP first-use reset FPSCR; cold FP activation and physical FP-context behavior are not proven. No FP setup instruction is added to firmware.",
    "Saved integer/FP registers, SP, masks, FPSCR, guards, reserved bytes and write widths/order/values checked. Caller scratch, APSR and private frames excluded. Modeled status sweeps observe full-word nonzero normalization in the compiled callback.",
    "Canonical writable state/workspace totals1687 bytes and coefficient arrays48 readonly bytes. Future initialization/calculation must reuse these owners. The descriptor coefficient labels do not establish the calculation algorithm.",
    "The top-level shutdown controller, native algorithm initialization/calculation, physical sensors, concurrency, final executable linking/startup and boot remain open. Relocatable composition is not bootable firmware."
  ],
